        // Contract visible in BooleanUtils.toBoolean(String): it accepts case-insensitive variants
        // of "on", "yes", and "true" and returns true for all of them. A patch that merely avoids
        // the crash by skipping the branch or changing control flow could silently return false for
        // some valid case variants. We therefore compare a fuzzed case-variant against the canonical
        // lower-case token using only real library calls on both sides.
        String canonical;
